From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:39:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ExactLimbSigns: the plane side of an integer point as a
 kernel of its own

The far point of a ray in front_crossings is an integer point (W = 1): its side is
A X + B Y + C Z - D. A kernel for that form replaces the constant W at the call site, so the
D term is covered by the kernel's test against BigInteger (cases where D decides the sign); a
far-from-origin input joins the operation-level test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AaGT5CdtKaF4p9ewMMrjAm
